1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=157042654 Find A Grave]: '''Esther Leonora Bryne Krueger'''. Birth: Mar. 5, 1899 in Valley City, Barnes County, North Dakota, USA. Death: Aug. 25, 1957 in Jamesto
2 CONC wn, Stutsman County, North Dakota, USA. Burial: Highland Home Cemetery, Jamestown, Stutsman County, North Dakota, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary (Jamestown, North Dakota Newspaper - Obituary, 1947):<br/>
2 CONT Mrs. '''Esther Krueger''', 58, 403 5th Avenue N. E., died Sunday at 10.35 p.m. at Trinity Hospital, Jamestown, after being a patient for two and a half hours, having suffered a heart attack at her home Sunday evening.<br/>
2 CONT Mrs. Krueger was born at Valley City on March 5, 1889, the daughter of Mr. and Mrs Gabriel Bryne. She attended school at Kathryn and in Barnes County. Miss Bryne came To Jamestown in 1917, and this has been her home since. Henry K
2 CONC rueger and Miss Bryne were married in Jamestown, March 18th, 1918. She was a member of the Trinity Lutheran Church and a past president of the Trinity ladies aid.<br/>
2 CONT Surviving are three children, Donald Krueger and Mrs. Kenneth Shank (Lois), Jamestown, and Gerald Krueger, St. Paul, Minn., four grandchildren, six sisters, Mrs. Matha Bolme, Jamestown; Mrs. Mary Birklid, Fort Ransom, N.D., Mrs. L
2 CONC ena Helland, Moose Jaw, Sask, Canada; Mrs. John Wenneson, Litchville, N.D., Mrs. Annie Shefte, Harvey, N.D., and Mrs. Ted Solheim, Fingal, N. D.<br/>
2 CONT Funeral services held on Wednesday at 2.00 p.m. at Trinity Lutheran Church with Rev. J. A. Nestingen, pastor, in charge. Burial in Highland Home Cemetery.<br/>
2 CONT Those who attended the funeral of Mrs. Esther Krueger on Wednesday were, Mrs. Mary Birklid and Mrs. Nels Jenson of Fort Ransom, Mr. and Mrs. Ernie Solheim of Minneapolis, Mr. and Mrs. Lars Birklid of Fargo, Mr. and Mrs. Edgar Birk
2 CONC lid, Ralph Birklid and Mr. and Mrs. Ted Solheim. Mrs. Krueger was a sister of Mrs. Mary Birklid and Mrs. Ted Solheim.
