1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Klepp Gards- og ættesoga gjenom 400 år, 1519-1900, Hauge, side 117, nr. 14.b
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Klepp Gards- og ættesoga gjenom 400 år, 1519-1900, Hauge, side 117, nr. 14'''
2 CONT Eilef Reierson, son åt nr. 13, f. 17/12 1834, d. 18/11 1907,
2 CONT G. 26/8 1858 m. Elen Tabitta Abrahamsd., Fjogstad nr. 21i, f. 20/8 1836, d. 28/6 1924.
2 CONT Born:
2 CONT * a. Jorina, f. 13/8 1860, g. m. Eilert Eivindson, n. Braut nr. 55.
2 CONT * b. Rasmus, f. 23/9 1865, USA.
2 CONT * c. Elen Elisabet, f. 21/5 1870, ug.
2 CONT * d. Anna, f. 11/12 1871, g. m. Tore Jensson, Lunde 56, Høyland.
2 CONT * e. Arnt, f. 19/3 1874, USA., d. 1/1 1924.
2 CONT * f. Regina, f. 8/3 1863, g. m. Ola Johannes Olson, s. Braut nr. 20.
2 CONT Reier fekk skøyte på farsgarden 28/10 1859, og 1862 gjekk det frå halvparten til br. nr. 3, og skylda vart då 2,53 mark, førd til 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT PEQUOT LAKES - Funeral services were held Monday for Rasmus Elef Hauge in Our Savior's Lutheran church. Burial was in the family plot of Our Savior's Lutheran cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Hauge died Dec. 23, in Los Angeles, Calif.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Stavanger, Norway, Sept. 23, 1865, he came to America in 1884 and settled near Huxley, Iowa. He married Josephine Olsen April 14, 1894, in Nevada, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1912 the family moved to Elmore, Minn, and in 1917 to a farm east of Pequot Lakes in Ideal township. During the last few months he had been living with a son Roy, in Los Angeles.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by three daughters, Mrs. Edwin (Rose) Holm of Elmore; Mrs. Orville (Ruth) Aas of The Dalles, Ore., and Mrs. Arthur (Alice) Hartwig of Hutchinson, Minn; two sons, Edward of Pequot Lakes and Roy of Los Angeles; two si
2 CONC sters, Mrs. Rasmus Sandwick of McCallsburg, Iowa, and Anne Lune in Norway; 22 grandchildren and 22 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relatives from a distance attending the funeral services were Mrs. Elwin Holm and son, Ray, of Elmore; Mrs. Orville Aas of The Dalles, Ore.; Mr. and Mrs. Arthur Hartwig and daugher, Barbara, and son James, of Hutchinson; Elmer Hau
2 CONC ge of Hutchinson; Elmer Hauge of Brainerd; Elwin Hauge of St. Paul and Gerald Hauge of the U.S. Navy.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
