1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ethel Hilma Sele (Higgin) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth:  Oct. 8, 1915 Lake Bronson Kittson County Minnesota, USA  Death:  Feb. 3, 2010 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethel Sele died peacefully Feb. 3, 2010 at the age of 94.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born on Oct. 8, 1915 to Ida and Albert Higgin in Lake Bronson, Minn. She graduated from Lake Bronson High School. She married George Sele in 1934. They moved to Hallock, Minn. in 1940. She was very active at Grace Lutheran
2 CONC  Church, PTA and was instrumental in founding Hallock Public Library. She and her husband avidly followed the activities of their three sons. She was an amazing Scandinavian cook, to the delight of her family and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT After her husband died in 1967, she moved to Bend, Ore. where her son Gene and his family lived. She taught Kindergarten, owned a restaurant and sold real estate. Ethel's passions were her home, garden and art. She was an accompli
2 CONC shed painter and potter and was a member of the Oregon Water Color Society. She was a published poet and shot story author and loved to travel to visit family and friends. Ethel moved to Portland in 2004 to be closer to family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was preceded in death by her husband George and her three brothers, Harold, Raymond and Richard. She is survived by her three sons, Gene, Portland, Ore.; Gary, Irving Texas; Michael, St. Paul, Minn.; 10 grandchildren and 21 gr
2 CONC eat grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT A "Celebration of Life" was held at Pilgrim Lutheran Church, Beaverton, Ore. Feb. 20. In lieu of flowers donations can be made to Hallock Public Library, Hallock, Minn. 56728. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   George Sele (1907 - 1967)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Greenwood Cemetery  Hallock Kittson County Minnesota, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: ShaneO Record added: Feb 25, 2010 
