3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}    Doris Irene Sele    
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Doris Irene Sele, 81, of Bemidji, formerly of Lake Bronson, MN, died on Friday, April 23rd 2004, at North Country Nursing and Rehabilitation Center. Doris was born on December 31st, 1922, to Selmer and Selma Locken in Hazelton Tow
2 CONC nship. She graduated from Lake Bronson High School. On May 4th, 1941 she married Stanley Sele. She lived in the Lake Bronson area, and worked as a secretary for the Lake Bronson and Karlstad school districts. Doris and Stanley own
2 CONC ed and operated a drive inn restaurant and had a bulk fuel business. She was a life long member of Zion Lutheran Church in Lake Bronson. She enjoyed crafts and to grow flowers, and was involved in church and community activities. 
2 CONC She moved to Bemidji in February 2001. Doris is survived by her daughter, Diane (Dale) Engstrom of Kingman, AZ; her son, Douglas (Carol) Sele of Bemidji, MN; five grandchildren; three great-grandchildren; three sisters, Marilyn Au
2 CONC bertin and Eleanore Lang, both of Spokane, WA, and Sandy (Chris) Martin of Lake Heron, NM. She is preceded in death by her parents, two brothers, Russell Locken and Kenneth Locken, and her husband, Stanley Sele. Services will be h
2 CONC eld at Zion Lutheran Church, Lake Bronson, at 10:30 am on Monday, April 26th, with burial following in Riverside Cemetery, Lake Bronson. A visitation will be held at Adamson-Austin-Hughes Funeral Home in Hallock, MN, from 6 pm-8 p
2 CONC m on Sunday with a prayer service at 7:00 pm. Dan Matz, presiding; Lenore Olson, organist and Marjorie Hawk, soloist. Casket bearers will be Odeen Anderson, Bob Rich, Rodger Hultgren, Vergil Poole, Larry Sele and Harvey Baker.  Pu
2 CONC blished in the Grand Forks Herald on 4/25/2004.  
2 CONT
