1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptized 10 January 1869: [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20050422010817 Beiarn, Ministerial book no. 846A02 (1837-1872), Born and baptized 1869, page 114]: No. 2: Born 21 Febr. 1868: '''Eilert Christian'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Note: There's something wrong with either his birthdate or date of baptism in that record. Every other record shows that he's born 21. February ''1869'', but if that is correct he cannot have been baptized 10. January. He cannot 
2 CONC have been born 21. February 1868 as the record states either, as that would've been to close to his elder brother born August 1867. REM
2 CONT
2 CONT Confirmation in 1884, No. 11: https://www.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070209620399
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://digitalarkivet.arkivverket.no/en-gb/ft/person/pf01052423000018 1875 census for Beiarn]: '''Ellert Larsen %Johnsen%''', born 1869 in Beieren. Residence: Birkelid.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://bdel.no/index.php?option=com_content&view=category&id=52&Itemid=93 Birkelisidene - The Eilert Branch]: In 1893 '''Eilert Kristian Larsen Birklid''', born February 21, 1869, emigrated to America with his brother Jacob. It i
2 CONC s somewhat difficult to follow his track, but he stayed for some years in Ransom County in North Dakota. There he became married the first time, their first two children were born, and his first wife Kristine Dorthea passed away. 
2 CONC She arrived in North Dakota in 1894, together with her sister Oline Andersen, her husband Kristen Andersen and their children.<br/>
2 CONT In the 1900 census Eilert stayed as a widower with his brother Jacob in Preston Township, but his eldest daughter Elida is not found in that census. But it is to be sure - according to the son of EIida's cousin, Richard Birklid - 
2 CONC that Elida stayed at Oline and Kristen Fjeld's in the 1900 census. (Kristen Andersen changed his surname to Fjeld). In the 1910 and 1920 censuses she is counted with this family. In 1905 Eilert took a trip home to Norway, and when
2 CONC  he went back to America his youngest brother Elias joined him. According to the family, to his mother's deepest sorrow.<br/>
2 CONT Eilert was married once more, to Anna Berkness from Minnesota. Probably they have stayed some years in Minnesota, because their only daughter Dorothy Imogene is born there. They moved to McGregor in North Dakota and stayed there f
2 CONC or many years. They are counted in McGregor in both the 1915 and the 1920 censuses. Some time they moved to Kent in the state of Washington, where they lived their last years. Eilert died on November 20, 1938, and Anna on May 22, 
2 CONC 1941. They are both buried at Meridian Cemetery in Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=5227342 Find a grave]: Obituary:<br/>
2 CONT ''Kent News-Journal'', Nov. 24, 1938, p-1:<br/>
2 CONT Funeral services for '''Eilert L. Birklid''', age 69, of 620 Fifth avenue south, will be held Friday afternoon at two o'clock from the chapel of the Kent Funeral Home.<br/>
2 CONT Mr. Birklid, a retired farmer, died at his home Sunday night. For the past two years he has made his home in Kent. For two years previous to moving to Kent he resided in the East Hill district, coming from North Dakota four years 
2 CONC ago.<br/>
2 CONT He was born February 21, 1869 in Norway.<br/>
2 CONT Burial will be made in the Kent cemetery.<br/>
2 CONT He is survived by his widow, ''Anna Birklid''; two daughters, Miss Imogene Birklid of Kent and Mrs. J. H. Snyder of Saskatchewan, Canada; four brothers, E. B. Birklid of Kent, Jacob L. Birklid of Lisbon, North Dakota, and two brot
2 CONC hers in Norway; and by four sisters in Norway."<br/>
2 CONT ''(From FAG member Mark Vernon)''
2 CONT
2 CONT Name on grave: '''Eliert Birklid'''.
